          wrongTurn: 'The wrong turn is describing what a rule does, because it reads like an explanation and takes no understanding to write. The test is whether you can say what would change if it were deleted.',
          tradeoff: 'Choosing the rules you are least sure about means the step takes longer and occasionally shows you that part of your stylesheet is doing nothing at all.',
